      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T13:06:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The service VM/RKP VM is supposed to be hardcoded and it will be bundled with pvmfw, so that we can leverage the trust of pvmfw to the service VM.\n\n\u003e Instead of hard-coding a hash into pvmfw, can\u0027t we use a vbmeta property to tag the image as a service VM?\n\nI don\u0027t think so. As we want to leverage the trust of pvmfw to service VM, it\u0027s not secure with a vbmeta property, anyone can add a property and claim to be the service VM.",
